{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Exponential","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.NatInt","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.GroupWithZero.Unbundled.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.PhiBSArgumentIdentification"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.gf_three_term_of_sq_dominated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.gf_three_term_of_sq_dominated","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L302-L331","doc":"**Capstone: the three-term functional equation holds at EVERY `w ≠ 0`**\nfor square-dominated winding rows — the `gf_three_term` `HasSum`\nhypotheses are discharged by entirety, so the relation among the `tsum`s\nholds on all of `ℂ*` with no continuation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.summable_winding_of_sq_dominated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.summable_winding_of_sq_dominated","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L263-L299","doc":"**Entirety of square-dominated winding families.** If\n`|c e| ≤ A·ρ^{(natAbs e)²}` with `0 < ρ < 1`, then `Σ_e c e · wᵉ`\nconverges absolutely for EVERY `w ≠ 0`: the winding generating function\nis entire on `ℂ*`. This is the machine-checked consequence of the\nquadratic-lead decay; no analytic continuation is ever needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.A_omega_eq_tsum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.A_omega_eq_tsum","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L204-L209","doc":"The constant Stokes coefficient of a winding-refined channel is the\n`tsum` of its winding family (derived from the `HasSum` field). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.A_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.A_total","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L201-L201","doc":"The base channel's constant is the `w = 1` total of the family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.A_family_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.A_family_symm","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L199-L199","doc":"Amphichiral symmetry of the family (4₁: `I(0,e) = I(0,−e)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.A_family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.A_family","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L197-L197","doc":"The per-winding-class Stokes coefficient family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.mk","kind":"ctor","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L194-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.toSDeformedVolumeChannel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding.toSDeformedVolumeChannel","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L194-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.SDeformedVolumeChannelWinding","kind":"class","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L188-L201","doc":"**Winding-refined Stokes channel** (bean qou-awpk Lean item): the Stokes\ncoefficient carried per winding class `e ∈ ℤ` (the GGM peacock lattice; for\n4₁ the extracted family is `I(0,e)` of the qou-awpk probe), amphichirally\nsymmetric, whose total is the base channel's constant `A_ω` — i.e. the\nconstant-A_ω channel is the `w = 1` (complete-structure) evaluation of the\nwinding family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.pairedWindowSum_unit_sheet_im_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.pairedWindowSum_unit_sheet_im_zero","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L160-L185","doc":"**Unit-sheet bar-even lemma** (#4433 structural result, formalized): a\nreal winding family in paired form — `c₀ + Σ_{e=1}^{N} c_e·(wᵉ + w⁻ᵉ)` —\nevaluated on the unit sheet `w = e^{iθ}` is real: its imaginary part\nvanishes identically. Amphichirality therefore forbids any bar-odd part\nof the winding-refined Stokes coefficient without RADIAL deformation\n(`|w| ≠ 1`) — the corpus structure `𝔲 = ln q₀ + iϑ` needs both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.gf_three_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.gf_three_term","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L87-L158","doc":"**The winding generating-function three-term functional equation**\n(conditional on the annihilator class). For `s > 0`, `w ≠ 0`, and `HasSum`\nhypotheses for the three rows at their arguments — row `m` at `w`, row\n`m−1` at `w/s`, row `m+1` at `s·w` — the sums satisfy\n\n  `c₋ · F_{m−1}(w/s) + P_m(w) · F_m(w) + c₊ · F_{m+1}(s·w) = 0`\n\nwith `c₋ = −s^{m+1}w + s^{−m−1}w⁻¹`, `c₊ = −s^{m−1}w + s^{−m+1}w⁻¹`, and\n`P_m` the middle Laurent polynomial. Since `|1/s| > 1` at the substrate,\nsolving for `F_{m−1}(w/s)` is the exact outward continuation step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.FourOneIndexAnnihilated.rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.FourOneIndexAnnihilated.rel","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.FourOneIndexAnnihilated.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.FourOneIndexAnnihilated.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.FourOneIndexAnnihilated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.WindingGFTransform.FourOneIndexAnnihilated","kind":"class","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/WindingGFTransform.lean#L55-L74","doc":"**The 4₁ index annihilator (DGG eq C.7), expanded scalar form** — a\nconditional class carrying the literature input. `s` is `√q̃` (so `q̃ = s²`\nand the paper's `q^{k/2}` weights are `s^k`), and `I m e` is the real value\nof the 3d-index at charge `(m,e)` (e.g. at a fixed evaluation point of the\nq-series). The ten-term identity is the mechanical expansion of\n\n  `L̂₄₁ = (q^{½}M̂ − q^{−½}M̂⁻¹)·ℓ̂⁻¹ − (M̂ − M̂⁻¹)(M̂² + M̂⁻² − M̂ − M̂⁻¹ − q − q⁻¹)\n         + (q^{−½}M̂ − q^{½}M̂⁻¹)·ℓ̂`\n\nwith the trefoil-calibrated actions `M̂f(m,e) = q^{m/2}f(m,e−1)`,\n`ℓ̂f(m,e) = −q^{e/2}f(m+1,e)`; the expansion is cross-checked to 1e−71\nagainst the composed operator on certified engine values (qou-3bp8 W1). ","signatureChunk":0}]}